[[Lieutenant]] '''Oxixo''' was a [[human]] who served the [[Galactic Empire]] as a [[Imperial Starfighter Pilot|TIE fighter pilot]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]]. In [[1 BBY]], he was flying a [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter]] as a sentry in the [[Alderaan system]] when the [[YT-1300 light freighter]] known as the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'' [[Rescue of Princess Leia|escaped]] from the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]]. Oxixo attacked the ''Falcon'' but was [[Death|killed]] when his [[starfighter]] was destroyed by the [[freighter]]'s [[AG-2G quad laser cannon|laser cannons]].

==Biography==
{{Quote|That's it. We did it.|Luke Skywalker celebrates killing Oxixo and the other pilots|audio=Luke-WeDidIt-ANH.flac|<ref name="A New Hope" />}}
[[File:FalconDeathStarEscape.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Oxixo pursued the ''Millennium Falcon'' in the Alderaan system, where he and his fellow pilots were killed.]]
Oxixo<ref name="EEarth" /> was a [[human]]<ref name="Updated and Expanded" /> [[Imperial Starfighter Pilot|TIE fighter pilot]] who served in the [[Imperial Starfighter Corps|Starfighter Corps]] of the [[Imperial Navy]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]]<ref name="A New Hope" /> with the [[military rank]] of [[lieutenant]].<ref name="EEarth" /> In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> he<ref name="EEarth" /> was stationed on board the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] [[battle station]] while it was located in the [[Alderaan system]] following the [[Destruction of Alderaan|destruction]] of the [[planet]] [[Alderaan]]. When the [[YT-1300 light freighter]] known as the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'' [[Rescue of Princess Leia|escaped]] from the [[Death Star]] carrying the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|rebel]] [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], Oxixo was [[pilot]]ing one of several [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter]]s acting as sentry craft in the Alderaan [[Star system|system]].<ref name="A New Hope" />

Four TIEs, including Oxixo's [[starfighter]], attacked the ''Falcon'' and managed to score several hits on it.<ref name="A New Hope" /> After the TIE formation scattered wide,<ref name="Odyssey">''[[The Odyssey of Star Wars: An Epic Poem]]''</ref> Oxixo [[Death|perished]] in the attack as all four starfighters were destroyed by the [[freighter]]'s [[AG-2G quad laser cannon|laser cannons]], which were manned by the ship's [[captain]], [[Han Solo]], and passenger [[Luke Skywalker]].<ref name="A New Hope" />

==Personality and traits==
By the [[time]] of his death, Oxixo was not a rookie.<ref name="Odyssey" />

==Equipment==
Oxixo carried an [[E-11 medium blaster rifle]]<ref name="Figure">{{HasbroCite|set=Star Wars: The Black Series|pack=Imperial Forces|altlink=https://www.rebelscum.com/hasbro-the-black-series-6-inch-imperial-forces-entertainment-earth-exclusive-multipack.asp}}</ref> and wore a [[Color|black]] Imperial pilot's [[Flight suit|uniform]] with a distinctive silver crest painted on the [[helmet]] that distinguished him from other members of his [[squadron]].<ref name="EEarth" /> The helmet also bore his name in [[High Galactic]].<ref name="A New Hope" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Oxixo.jpg|thumb|right|250px|The name Oxixo was first used on a 2010 action figure.]]
Oxixo first appeared in the [[1977]] [[original trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']].<ref name="A New Hope" /> Oxixo's closeup in his [[cockpit]] was filmed on Stage 8 at [[Elstree Studios]] between [[June 29]] and [[July 16]], [[1976]].<ref name="MakingOf">''[[The Making of Star Wars]]''</ref> The name Oxixo was first used in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity for an action figure in the "Battle Over Endor" playset released by [[Hasbro]] as part of their [[2010]] ''[[Star Wars: Shadows of the Dark Side]]'' toy line. The figure was of a [[Oxixo/Legends|TIE fighter pilot]] bearing Oxixo's distinctive silver helmet crest but was described by the set's packaging as taking part in the [[Battle of Endor/Legends|Battle of Endor]],<ref name="Hasbro">{{HasbroCite|set=Star Wars: Shadows of the Dark Side|pack=(Toys R Us Exclusive) Battle Over Endor (1 of 2)|altlink=https://www.rebelscum.com/TVCEXBattleOverEndor1.asp}}</ref> making it a distinct character from the pilot who perishes in ''A New Hope''.<ref name="A New Hope" />

In [[2015]], Hasbro released an action figure labeled as Oxixo in the [[canon]] ''[[Star Wars: The Black Series]]'' line as part of an "Imperial Forces" set sold exclusively by [[Wikipedia:Entertainment Earth|Entertainment Earth]]. While the set listing on Entertainment Earth's website described Oxixo as flying in at the Battle of Endor,<ref name="EEarth" /> as per his previous figure,<ref name="Hasbro" /> the set packaging explicitly identified him as one of the four pilots shot down in the Alderaan system in ''A New Hope''. This article assumes the packaging to be correct.<ref name="Figure" />

